  "asserts": {
   "ribbonBands": "P1. Bands are the distinct tops (6 px) of the visible [data-ribbon-group] elements; mode one: exactly one; two: exactly two; oneOrTwo: one or two (the count is in the detail); stacked: seven bands and every group as wide as the panel (4 px). The page and the panel do not scroll sideways. With one band every group is at most maxBandHeight high. The group names ([data-group-label] text) in document order equal `order`.",
   "rowFill": "P1. Rows are the [data-row] elements of the visible groups that hold at least one visible control. For each: the right edge of its last visible child is within edgeTol of the group's inner right edge (the group's right edge less its border and padding); the gap between neighbouring visible children is at most gapMax; at least one child has data-stretch. Nothing is centred (the first child's left edge is the group's inner left edge within 2 px).",
   "ribbonSizes6": "P1. Visible buttons, inputs and selects of [data-ribbon-panel] except spin arrows ([data-spin]) are small[0] to small[1] high; buttons marked [data-fixed-icon] are iconWidth wide; every [data-row-label] has a computed font size within rowLabel; every control's text size within controlFont; every [data-group-label] within groupName (0.5 px tolerance, inclusive).",
   "menuState": "P5. The button `button`: aria-expanded true and a role menu element visible (open true) or aria-expanded not true and no visible menu (open false); focus: inside means document.activeElement is inside the menu, button means it is the button.",
   "menuContents": "P5. The open menu of `button`: its menuitemradio items between the headings Page colours and Standard colours are, by aria-label, equal to the document's distinct colours up to 16 in first-use order when pageColours is document (the runner reads the original files in their order, primary first, matching #rgb, #rrggbb, #rrggbbaa, rgb(), rgba(), hsl() and hsla() in text order, lower case, 6-digit hex, no duplicates); the items after Standard colours are the 8 colours of `standard`; the menu has an item `none` (when not null) and an item `more`; `submenus` maps a submenu trigger (menuitem with aria-haspopup) to the labels of its items, found by opening it.",
   "menuChecked": "P5. In the open menu (reopened if needed) the item `item` has aria-checked equal to `checked`.",
   "menuFocus": "P5. The focused element is a menu item whose accessible name is `name`.",
   "submenuOpen": "P5. The submenu trigger `name` has aria-expanded true (open) and a visible submenu, or not.",
   "exportsEqual": "P5. The two snapshotExport texts (every file) are byte for byte equal and differ from the original source.",
   "fontPresets": "P5. Opening the arrow of the font size box (button Font size presets) shows menu items whose names are exactly `values` in order; the menu is left open.",
   "holdSteps": "P1. After holdButton, the element's `q` changed from `from` by a whole number of 1 px steps between min and max.",
   "togglePressed": "P5. The button `name` has aria-pressed equal to `pressed`.",
   "lineHeightRatio": "P1. The element's computed line-height divided by its computed font-size equals `value` within `tol`.",
   "disabledStyle": "P5. The named controls' computed color, background colour and opacity (a signature) are stored under `key`; with sameAs the signature equals the stored one, and every control is disabled.",
   "touchTargets": "P5. Every visible button, input, select and spin arrow ([data-spin]) of [data-ribbon] is at least `min` px high and wide.",
   "menuFits": "P5. The open menu lies inside the window horizontally (0.5 px) and, if taller than the window, scrolls inside (its overflow-y is auto or scroll); every item is at least itemMin high.",
